content:
The logs show 503s hitting the external payment-provider (E9), and the deploy at t=467 is 61 s before first symptoms at t=528 (E10). I need one more check to distinguish: did the deploy change how the provider is called (bad_deploy) or is the provider itself down independently? Checking payment-provider reachability/status from another angle — specifically whether any successful provider calls occurred between t=467 and t=528 — would separate these.

```json
{
  "investigate": [
    {
      "tool": "sql",
      "query": "SELECT status, COUNT(*) as cnt, MIN(created_at) as first_at, MAX(created_at) as last_at FROM payments WHERE created_at >= 467 ORDER BY status;",
      "why": "If payments succeeded between t=467 and t=528 (after the deploy but before the errors), the provider was reachable post-deploy and the outage is an external_dependency failure. If all payments failed from t=467 onward, the deploy is more likely the cause."
    }
  ],
  "hypotheses": [
    {
      "service": "payment-provider",
      "kind": "external_dependency",
      "mechanism": "The external payment-provider began returning HTTP 503 responses around t=528, independently of the payment-service deploy, causing all payment attempts to fail.",
      "supporting": ["E4", "E7", "E9", "E2", "E3"],
      "refuting": ["E5"],
      "explains": ["M2_error_burst"],
      "repair_plan": []
    },
    {
      "service": "payment-service",
      "kind": "bad_deploy",
      "mechanism": "The v1.0.1 dependency-version update deployed at t=467 introduced a breaking change in provider communication that manifests as 503 errors from the payment-provider.",
      "supporting": ["E5", "E4", "E9", "E2", "E3"],
      "refuting": [],
      "explains": ["M2_error_burst"],
      "repair_plan": [
        {"action": "rollback_service", "params": {"service": "payment-service"}}
      ]
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Payment-service is receiving 503s from the external payment-provider starting t=528; one more investigation step is needed to determine whether the provider failed independently or the t=467 deploy broke the integration."
}
```
